{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/531915-can-you-recommend-a-new-fantasy-crpg","id":531915,"title":"Can you recommend a new fantasy cRPG?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-29T06:30:28-07:00","id":531915,"title":"Can you recommend a new fantasy cRPG?","content":"When I say new, I mean new to me. I've played:<br /> * the five core Elder Scrolls games. They're flexible and the lore is rich, but I find them a bit cut and dry compared with other settings. From TESIII onwards they've lacked mystery and things that go bump in the night.<br /> * the White Wolf Vampire games. I found Bloodlines more engaging and enjoyable all round.<br /> * Dragon Age: Origins. Good setting and sympathetic central characters, but it somehow feels a bit detached. I don't how to explain that.<br /> * The Witcher. Delightful setting, art direction and story.<br /> <br /> Ideally, I'd like to play a mage or something like one. I'm quite happy with any time setting so long as it's detailed or real life/mythological details can be assumed to fill some blanks, but at the same time, there's a poorly understood spiritual world. Anthropology is important to me too though. I'm more interested in the effects a cult has on a community than whether their beliefs are true or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T08:19:58-07:00","id":531965,"title":"","content":"Pillars of Eternity. Its as close to old school Black Isle as you can get. Very similar to Baldur's Gate, Icewind Dale, Planescape","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T08:22:34-07:00","id":531967,"title":"","content":"You might like Shadow of Mordor. The character is more a warrior than a mage, but LotR is a <i>pretty detailed</i> setting. The gameplay basically epitomizes mechanics taken from the Batman Arkham games and Assassin's Creed (or so I'm told, as I never played the later). Also, you can specifically observe remnants from the past (broken tools, lost letters, et cetera) to unveil details of the local history and the people that lived there (it is similar to how it was done in the rebooted Tomb Raider, if you played that). The conflicts within the orc army as orcs vie for positions in the hierarchy are also fun to observe (and intervene).<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, I'll second the recommendation for Pillars of Eternity","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":868,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","user":"danelsan","date":". 05-30-2015, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T03:14:23-07:00","id":533015,"title":"","content":"Give Planescape: Torment a chance. Graphics are terrible, but a widescreen mod fixes that problem. Gameplay has its problems (combat is a slog, the utility of mental attributes strongly outweighs the utility of the Str-Dex-Con trio, which means you're better off as a caster, but you start out as a fighter and switching classes is its own quest, which might potentially cause you to lose out on quite a bit of xp), but it's just so fundamentally unlike any other RPG, it has to be experienced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":3443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","user":"aluminiumtrioxid","date":". 05-30-2015, 06:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T02:11:11-07:00","id":534145,"title":"","content":"Planescape: Torment is definitely my favorite RPG of all time. So, I can't recommend it enough. <br /> <br /> There's also Baldur's Gate and Baldur's Gate 2, both of which recently got remakes with updated graphics and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}